// =====================================================================================
// PaloAlto_tests.kql  --  parser tests that exercise the REAL deployed code
// =====================================================================================
// WHAT CHANGED / WHY
//   These tests feed synthetic CEF rows into the ACTUAL production parser
//   (PaloAlto_CEF_ParseRows) -- they do NOT re-implement the parse. So a change to
//   PaloAlto_CEF.kql that breaks extraction WILL fail a test here (no silent drift), and
//   there's no duplicated parse-kv schema to keep in sync.
//
// PREREQUISITE
//   Deploy PaloAlto_CEF.kql first (at least PaloAlto_CEF_ParseRows). The tests still touch
//   NO real tables -- they pass a datatable straight into the function.
//
// RESULTS (two tables)
//   A) Field assertions -- every row Passed == true, Details empty.
//   B) Invariant check  -- the non-Palo-Alto (Cisco) row is dropped and exactly the 4
//      Palo Alto rows survive. This is a property the parser must hold; it is not an
//      input/expected value we supply.
//
//   Sample values are FAKE but representative (RFC 5737/1918 IPs, example users).
// =====================================================================================

let FakeSyslog = datatable(TestName:string, TimeGenerated:datetime, Computer:string, SyslogMessage:string)
[
  "TRAFFIC_drop_13.5", datetime(2026-06-15T14:58:03Z), "fw-edge-01",
